IMPORT policy

-- Standing preamble (applies to every query below): assuming all other
-- conditions are met and no other exclusions apply, and that the agreement
-- has been signed and the premium paid on time. So every fact the question
-- text does not mention is set here to a value that satisfies conditions
-- and avoids exclusions: age 40 (well under the age-80 exclusion), zero
-- months elapsed for any unmentioned time, no fraud/misrepresentation/
-- withholding, and no unmentioned excluded-cause.

-- Q1: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized by burns suffered while
-- doing my duty as a firefighter?
-- Hospitalization is caused by firefighter service -- excluded by 2.1(3).
q1 MEANS HospitalizationClaim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`             IS 40
    `hospitalization time`               IS 0
    `caused by skydiving`                IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`         IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS TRUE
    `caused by police service`           IS FALSE
    `fraudulent`                         IS FALSE
    `misrepresented`                     IS FALSE
    `withheld information`               IS FALSE
    `wellness visit time`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS 0

#EVAL `covered` q1

-- Q2: will my policy apply if I am 78 years old at the time of
-- hospitalization?
-- 78 is below the age-80 exclusion threshold in 2.1(5); cause of
-- hospitalization is not mentioned, so no cause-based exclusion applies.
q2 MEANS HospitalizationClaim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`             IS 78
    `hospitalization time`               IS 0
    `caused by skydiving`                IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`         IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`           IS FALSE
    `fraudulent`                         IS FALSE
    `misrepresented`                     IS FALSE
    `withheld information`               IS FALSE
    `wellness visit time`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS 0

#EVAL `covered` q2

-- Q3: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for pneumonia 5 months
-- after the policy's effective date, and my age at the time of
-- hospitalization is 65?
-- Pneumonia is not an excluded cause; age 65 and 5 months are both well
-- clear of every threshold in the policy (age 80, term of 12 months).
q3 MEANS HospitalizationClaim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`             IS 65
    `hospitalization time`               IS 5
    `caused by skydiving`                IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`         IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`           IS FALSE
    `fraudulent`                         IS FALSE
    `misrepresented`                     IS FALSE
    `withheld information`               IS FALSE
    `wellness visit time`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS 0

#EVAL `covered` q3

-- Q4: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to a fall while
-- traveling abroad and I had given confirmation of my wellness visit 8
-- months after the policy's effective date?
-- A fall is not an excluded cause, and 3.1.1 covers the insured anywhere in
-- the world -- but confirmation at month 8 is later than the 7-month
-- deadline in 1.3, so the condition fails and the policy is canceled
-- under 1.2, regardless of the cause of hospitalization.
q4 MEANS HospitalizationClaim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`             IS 40
    `hospitalization time`               IS 0
    `caused by skydiving`                IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`         IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`           IS FALSE
    `fraudulent`                         IS FALSE
    `misrepresented`                     IS FALSE
    `withheld information`               IS FALSE
    `wellness visit time`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS 8

#EVAL `covered` q4

-- Q5: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for punching my own face
-- to show off for my friends and I did not commit fraud or
-- misrepresentation?
-- No exclusion in 2.1 covers a self-inflicted, foolish injury of this kind,
-- and the query itself rules out the fraud/misrepresentation cancelation
-- ground in 1.2.
q5 MEANS HospitalizationClaim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`             IS 40
    `hospitalization time`               IS 0
    `caused by skydiving`                IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`         IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`           IS FALSE
    `fraudulent`                         IS FALSE
    `misrepresented`                     IS FALSE
    `withheld information`               IS FALSE
    `wellness visit time`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS 0

#EVAL `covered` q5

-- Q6: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to an injury sustained
-- while skydiving, my age at the time of hospitalization was 79, and proof
-- of my wellness visit was provided 6.5 months after the policy's
-- effective date?
-- Skydiving is squarely excluded by 2.1(1), independent of age (79 is
-- still under 80) and independent of the wellness-visit timing (6.5
-- months is still inside the 7-month confirmation deadline in 1.3, so that
-- condition is not itself a problem here).
q6 MEANS HospitalizationClaim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`             IS 79
    `hospitalization time`               IS 0
    `caused by skydiving`                IS TRUE
    `caused by military service`         IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`           IS FALSE
    `fraudulent`                         IS FALSE
    `misrepresented`                     IS FALSE
    `withheld information`               IS FALSE
    `wellness visit time`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS 6.5

#EVAL `covered` q6

-- Q7: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for a heart attack, proof
-- of the wellness visit was submitted 2 months after the policy's
-- effective date, and my age at the time of hospitalization was 75?
-- A heart attack is not an excluded cause; age 75 is under 80; and
-- confirmation at month 2 is comfortably inside both 1.3 deadlines.
q7 MEANS HospitalizationClaim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`             IS 75
    `hospitalization time`               IS 0
    `caused by skydiving`                IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`         IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`           IS FALSE
    `fraudulent`                         IS FALSE
    `misrepresented`                     IS FALSE
    `withheld information`               IS FALSE
    `wellness visit time`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS 2

#EVAL `covered` q7

-- Q8: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized after being injured in a
-- military training exercise, the hospitalization occurred within the
-- policy term, and I did not commit fraud?
-- The injury arises directly out of military service, so 2.1(2) excludes
-- it outright; "within the policy term" and "no fraud" only confirm that
-- no OTHER ground for refusal is present.
q8 MEANS HospitalizationClaim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`             IS 40
    `hospitalization time`               IS 0
    `caused by skydiving`                IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`         IS TRUE
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`           IS FALSE
    `fraudulent`                         IS FALSE
    `misrepresented`                     IS FALSE
    `withheld information`               IS FALSE
    `wellness visit time`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS 0

#EVAL `covered` q8

-- Q9: will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to my son biting me
-- in the ankle, proof of my wellness visit was provided 6 months after
-- the effective date, and I was serving as a police officer at the time
-- of hospitalization?
-- Being a police officer AT THE TIME is occupation/status, not causation:
-- 2.1(4) excludes injury "arising directly or indirectly out of ... service
-- in the police", and a son's bite is unconnected to police duty, so the
-- exclusion is not made out (`caused by police service` is FALSE here,
-- deliberately, even though the claimant is a police officer). Month 6 is
-- inside both 1.3 deadlines (<= 6 and <= 7).
q9 MEANS HospitalizationClaim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`             IS 40
    `hospitalization time`               IS 0
    `caused by skydiving`                IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`         IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`      IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`           IS FALSE
    `fraudulent`                         IS FALSE
    `misrepresented`                     IS FALSE
    `withheld information`               IS FALSE
    `wellness visit time`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation time`   IS 6

#EVAL `covered` q9
